   "game": null,
   "where": "League investigation",
   "text": "The league has finished its investigation of the Shredders (opened in week 8). The league's investigators concluded the allegation of a pay-for-injury program is substantiated. The club cooperated fully with the investigation. Investigators said senior staff were aware of the conduct. THE FINDINGS: investigators recovered messages in a Shredders defensive staff group chat offering $1,500 per opposing player knocked out of a game, and payment records show 8 payments to 5 players over the season. Opposing injuries of 2+ weeks in Shredders games: week 4, Gozie Hartlow (CB, Dales), 4 wks, calf; week 7, Chike Adamah (CB, Phenoms), 2 wks, groin; week 8, Aurelio Yorkshaw (DL, Rangers), 2 wks, high ankle sprain. Investigators tied Chike Adamah (Phenoms) to the program; the rest could not be linked to it.\n\nOriginal matter: The league is looking into allegations that Shredders defenders were offered cash for knocking opponents out of games. Investigators have requested internal messages. The club denied the allegation. Several opposing players left games with injuries this season.\n\nWHERE THINGS STAND. In week 8 you opened a formal investigation and made no ruling on the club. Anything you choose below is the ruling on the club.",
